WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.137
The re-read client does the checking.

2
00:00:02.137 --> 00:00:06.358
It lists the waiting findings
through ServiceNow's Table API,

3
00:00:06.358 --> 00:00:09.088
then re-reads each subject by its system.

4
00:00:09.088 --> 00:00:11.900
An ISC account is read by its ID.

5
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.813
An ISC identity is found with a Search.

6
00:00:14.813 --> 00:00:18.581
And an Entra user is read
through Microsoft Graph,

7
00:00:18.581 --> 00:00:22.075
which returns a 404 when
the user doesn't exist.

8
00:00:22.075 --> 00:00:25.775
Each read has its own least
permission, shown on the slide.

9
00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:29.625
Then the client compares what it read
with the finding's intended state.

10
00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:34.701
On a match, it closes the record with
the evidence: the query, the time,

11
00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:39.592
a SHA-256 hash of the response,
the intended state and the checker,

12
00:00:39.592 --> 00:00:42.637
and it attaches that evidence as JSON.

13
00:00:42.637 --> 00:00:46.350
On a mismatch, it reopens the
record with the differences.

14
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.270
And it writes nothing unless
you pass the apply option.
